---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const counted = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN);
---
<Base title="Privacy">
  <article class="container page-body">
    <div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>Your work stays yours.</h1><p>{counted ? 'No cookies, no tracking. Visits are counted without identifying you.' : 'No cookies, no analytics, no tracking.'}</p></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>This website.</h2><p>Fonts, screenshots and scripts are served with the site. Your theme preference and download release data are saved in your browser’s localStorage. Release data is cached for ten minutes.</p>
      <p>The download page calls GitHub’s public API from your browser to check for a release. GitHub receives that request under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy terms</a>. If the request fails, the page uses release data bundled with this site. Download links take you to GitHub.</p>
      <h2>The browser console.</h2><p>Your code runs locally in a worker on your device and is not sent anywhere. Share links store code in the URL fragment, which is not sent to the server. Anyone you give a share link can read the code it contains. The console has no access to your files.</p>
      <h2>The desktop app.</h2><p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/leoom-labs/matrust/blob/main/docs/privacy.md">desktop privacy documentation</a> for details about the app and benchmark output.</p>
      {counted && <><h2>Visit counts.</h2><p>Pages load Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views, referring sites, countries and page load times. It sets no cookies, uses no fingerprinting and does not track you across sites. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>. The browser console page does not load it, so your code and share links are never part of it.</p></>}
      <h2>Hosting.</h2><p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Requests for site files are subject to GitHub’s privacy terms.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
